{"title":"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae87c01e845fac366bd189f4bf6a048acaa445f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100i\\leq n &lt; 100(i + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />.  For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927ca6f264730b7f22ea5e06ee7ac6872819f94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/817e8c95374fa312fe4352b89b74c784329a9623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${400,401,402,\\ldots,499}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />.  How many of the sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8b51fc6a89fa08fcf8c9fb8caa8825e551b865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_0, S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> do not contain a perfect square?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The difference between consecutive squares is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f98f563ebe850ef9d0cf09d650b813304997145.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + 1)^2 - x^2 = 2x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />, which means that all squares above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/89614a5f77a6575ccf67b845f68f856459b01235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^2 = 2500$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> are more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> apart.\n</p><p>Then the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sets (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101ffba7cd802186ef12a3bb3aeb8ed4abf00ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_0,\\cdots S_{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />) each have at least one perfect square because the differences between consecutive squares in them are all less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/3/9b35d42f74b745f1069b2cf89af1141d8cf468ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$316$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23c887d71fce031e5c55e7623a24450befe061b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 &lt; 100000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"95\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1c9cc35374b57f3e393a898263c4cda825e912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> is the upper bound which all numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e081541a11745aba71590b5136070df63c6336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> must be less than), there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f8418196de3497cff87c46d58f76dc6b06b60923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$316 - 50 = 266$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"118\" height=\"13\" /> other sets after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc2d0205deeabb2ca14234d6ccfde270013392c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> that have a perfect square.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a6ebdcdd96dcb0ad74bcb6a08a9066a77352ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000 - 266 - 26 = \\boxed{708}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"189\" height=\"23\" /> sets without a perfect square.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6eBLXnzK0n4\">https://youtu.be/6eBLXnzK0n4</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I\" title=\"2008 AIME I\">2008 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017045456\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 178/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3602/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.008      1 -total\n 59.63%    9.545      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.73%    6.040      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6621:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017045456 and revision id 141370. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}